316:"Magnetic Field of a Toroidal Solenoid, Ampere's Law, Physics & Electromagnetism",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XWtscd-IoDU,Derives and applies the magnetic-field formula for a toroidal solenoid using Ampere's law.
318:Torque on a Current Loop In a Magnetic Field & Magnetic Dipole Moment - Physics,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-l-aajUS_Ik,Calculates the torque and magnetic dipole moment of a current loop in a uniform magnetic field and derives the torque formula for a current-carrying coil.
341:"Maxwell's Equations, Electromagnetic Waves, Displacement Current, & Poynting Vector - Physics",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mOEFTX9DAEw,"Covers Maxwell’s equations and electromagnetic waves, including electric and magnetic flux, displacement current in a capacitor, electric–magnetic field relationships, the Poynting vector, transferred energy, and field energy density."
344:Spherical Mirrors & The Mirror Equation - Geometric Optics,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=efPZ5uSDeuI,"Covers concave and convex mirrors, the mirror equation, focal length and curvature, image distance, magnification, image orientation and size, and concave-mirror ray diagrams."
348:"Thin Lens Equation, Optics, Converging Lens & Diverging Lens - Physics",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7ehfXmO42h8,"Applies the thin-lens equation to converging and diverging lenses, including image distance, real and virtual images, orientation, size, magnification, image height, and lens power."
361:ACT Math Test Prep,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SsA7rZ8kczM,"Reviews common ACT math problems in algebra, geometry, and trigonometry, including relevant formulas, worked solutions, and test-taking strategies."
363:Chemistry,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-KfG8kH-r3Y,"Introduces the periodic table, element families, ion charges, atoms and ions, ionic and molecular compounds, nomenclature, polyatomic ions, chemical formulas, isotopes, average atomic mass, and subatomic-particle counts."
364:"Geometry Introduction - Basic Overview - Review For SAT, ACT, EOC, Midterm Final Exam",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KtZai86htng,"Reviews geometry concepts including angles, measurement, perimeter, area, surface area, volume, and the properties and formulas of common two- and three-dimensional shapes."
365:Trigonometry For Beginners!,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PUB0TaZ7bhA,"Introduces sine, cosine, tangent, SOHCAHTOA, solving right triangles for missing sides, and finding missing angles with inverse trigonometric functions."

