{"lecture_id":"2026-06-25-M1-2","lecture_summary":"The lecture synchronizes translational and rotational motion to solve a rotating-disk bullet problem, emphasizing covariational reasoning, shared-time equations, dimensional checks, and solving symbolically first. It then derives inward radial acceleration for uniform circular motion, applies a_r = v²/r in a ranking example, and distinguishes radial, tangential, and total acceleration in nonuniform circular motion.","videos":[{"rank":1,"title":"Angular Velocity Physics Problems, Linear Speed, Frequency & Period","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d5VXZGinKSk","reason":"Provides the angular-motion foundation for the disk problem: angular displacement and speed, period and frequency, ω = 2π/T, and coordinating rotational timing with linear motion."},{"rank":2,"title":"Introduction to Centripetal Acceleration - Period, Frequency, & Linear Speed - Physics Problems","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZbLirQuT9uU","reason":"Best match for the main uniform-circular-motion section, covering changing velocity direction, inward radial acceleration, and calculations involving linear speed, period, and frequency."},{"rank":3,"title":"Non-Uniform Circular Motion Problems, Centripetal Acceleration & Tangential Acceleration, Physics","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XlvD5_0FVSc","reason":"Covers the distinct extension to nonuniform motion: separating radial and tangential acceleration and combining them to determine net acceleration."}],"coverage_gaps":["No strong match for the exact two-disk bullet synchronization problem or the derivation v = 2πD/(Tθ).","No relevant video explicitly teaches covariational reasoning by predicting how the result varies with D, T, and θ.","The symbolic-first workflow and dimensional/limiting checks are not specifically covered; the playlist’s dimensional-analysis videos focus on unit conversion.","The playlist metadata does not confirm coverage of the lecture’s similar-triangle vector derivation of a_r = v²/r or its four-case radial-acceleration ranking example."]}
